  "_comment": "Per-zone gathering node pools for OVERWORLD zones. 'slots' = candidate spawn points rolled per zone entry. 'active_percent' = fraction that actually spawn each visit. 'table' = weighted material pool. PROGRESSION DESIGN (audited 2026-10-26): Early zones (1-15) use Copper/Weakstone ore only; Tin creeps in at Northern Barrens (10-20); Iron first appears Southern Barrens (18-25) at weight 1; Iron becomes mid-weight in Ashenvale (20-32). NO Copper in Ashenvale - player is 20+ and has long graduated past it. NO Silver/Coal until Ashenvale. Mid herbs (Bruiseweed) first appear Central Barrens; Briarthorn/Liferoot appear Southern Barrens/Silverpine; Kingsblood/Goldthorn are Silverpine South / Ashenvale. Tirisfal (4-14) is early-only - no mid herbs or Ironbark. Fenris Isle (16-22) is newly added: herb/coastal-wood-rich wolf island. Wood: Ashwood/Oakheart early, Softpine/Ironbark mid (Silverpine+), Frostpine/Bramblewood late (Ashenvale). Bramblewood is Ashenvale-only (densest forest). Cave ore pools are derived from parent zone table by gathering_manager.py - not authored here. Town zones (Brill, Sepulcher, Astranaar, etc.) have no pool - same convention everywhere. HILLSBRAD (added 2026-10-27): Western Hillsbrad (20-24) and Eastern Hillsbrad (23-27) sit between Silverpine South and Ashenvale, so no Copper/Weakstone anywhere - the player is 20+. Iron is the staple in both and outweighs Tin. SILVER is deliberately broken out of the 'Ashenvale only' rule for Western Hillsbrad: Azurelode Mine is a silver mine in Classic and it is that zone's signature landmark, so silver at weight 2 there is the lore, not a power creep. Eastern Hillsbrad gets silver at 1 and the first Coal outside Ashenvale, befitting 23-27. Frostpine appears only in the east, under Alterac's peaks. Coastal materials (stranglekelp, driftwood, tideglass) are weighted to the WEST, which owns both the sea coasts; the east has only the short southern strand.",
